<BaseLayout title="Privacy Notice — TH Homes" description="How TH Homes handles personal information under Nigerian data protection law.">
  <section class="page-hero legal-hero"><div class="page-hero-inner"><h1>Privacy, clearly handled.</h1><p>How we collect, use and protect personal information when you visit this website or contact TH Homes.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><article class="section-inner legal-copy">
    <p class="legal-updated">Last reviewed: 23 November 2026</p>
    <h2>Our commitment</h2><p>TH Homes Projects is responsible for the personal information described in this notice. We handle it in line with the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023, including the principles of fairness, transparency, purpose limitation, data minimisation, accuracy, storage limitation and security.</p>
    <h2>Information we collect</h2><p>When you submit an enquiry, we may collect your name, email address, phone number, location and the project information you choose to provide. We may also receive limited technical information needed to deliver and secure the website. Please do not include sensitive personal information in a project brief.</p>
    <h2>Why we use it</h2><p>We use enquiry information to respond to you, assess project fit, route your request to the appropriate team and keep necessary business records. Our lawful basis will normally be taking steps at your request before a contract, performing a contract, complying with a legal obligation, or a legitimate interest that does not override your rights. We will ask for consent where Nigerian law requires it.</p>
    <h2>Sharing, transfers and retention</h2><p>We only share information with authorised staff and service providers that need it to provide the website or respond to your enquiry. Before using a provider outside Nigeria, we will apply the transfer safeguards required by Nigerian law. We keep information only for as long as necessary for the stated purpose, legal obligations and the resolution of disputes, then delete or anonymise it securely.</p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2><p>Subject to applicable law, you may ask to access, correct, erase or restrict your personal information, object to certain processing, request portability, withdraw consent, or ask for a human review of a solely automated decision. You may also complain to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission.</p>
    <h2>Contact us</h2><p>To exercise a privacy right or ask a question, use our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. We may need to verify your identity before acting on a request. This website is still using development contact details; verified privacy contact details must be added before launch.</p>
  </article></section>
</BaseLayout>
